outs:
- md5: abf12158e9d056051bad923a2cf80c06
  size: 48748
  hash: md5
  path: final_energy.parquet
meta:
  name:
    de: Mainz Endenergieverbrauch nach Sektor und Energietraeger
  identifier: mainz/final_energy
  metrics:
  - column_id: Value
    unit: MWh
  - column_id: quality
    unit: ''
  index_columns:
  - sector
  - energy_carrier
  - Year
  updated_at: '1788117968'
  sources:
  - name: EKA-RLP Datenservice Strom und Gas Mainz 2014-2024
    authority: Energieagentur Rheinland-Pfalz (EKA-RLP) -- Datenlieferservice 
      Kommunales Klimaschutzcontrolling; bilanzierungstool@energieagentur.rlp.de
    url:
    description: "Annual grid-bound final energy for Mainz: electricity and natural
      gas in kWh/a, split by consumer sector (private households, GHD, industry, municipal
      properties, street lighting, heat pumps, night-storage heating, agriculture
      and forestry, utility's own operations). Delivered 2026-03-31 and prepared by
      Kausal in AUFBEREITET_EKA-RLP-Datenservice_Strom_Gas_2014-24_geliefert20260331.xlsx.
      The electricity delivery combines GHD with industry; the split is estimated
      (see the workbook's own note).; Attachment: AUFBEREITET_EKA-RLP-Datenservice_Strom_Gas_2014-24_geliefert20260331.xlsx;
      Format: .xlsx; Licensing: Provided to the city for climate accounting; not public;
      Geographic Coverage: Mainz (AGS 07315000); Update Frequency: Annual; Date Last
      Updated: 2026-03-31; Updated by: EKA-RLP"
  - name: Klimaschutzplaner Export Mainz 1990-2024
    authority: Landeshauptstadt Mainz -- Grün- und Umweltamt; export from the 
      Klimaschutzplaner tool
    url:
    description: 'Historical BISKO final energy and emissions for Mainz as held in
      the Klimaschutzplaner, exported per sector sheet (Private Haushalte, GHD/Sonstige,
      Industrie, Kommunale Einrichtungen, Verkehr). Authoritative for 1990-2018 only:
      from 2020 the export carries Heizöl values identical to Erdgas, zeroes Fernwärme,
      Biomasse and Solarthermie, zeroes Kommunale Einrichtungen, and leaves 2024 empty.;
      Attachment: 073150000000_stationaer_1990-2024_data.xlsx; Format: .xlsx; Licensing:
      Provided to the city; not public; Geographic Coverage: Mainz (AGS 07315000);
      Update Frequency: Superseded -- no further updates expected; Date Last Updated:
      2026-01-27; Updated by: Landeshauptstadt Mainz'
  - name: Schätzung Sektor-Split Strom GHD/Industrie Mainz
    authority: Kausal
    url:
    description: 'Estimated share of industry within the combined GHD+industry electricity
      consumption reported by EKA-RLP. Derived in 2026 from German industry-sector
      energy statistics and employment statistics (national averages) applied to Mainz
      employment by branch. Factor 0.35. The source workbook carries the instruction
      to re-check every 2.5 to 5 years.; Attachment: Schätzung & Plausibilitätsprüfung
      von Energieverbrauch-Sektor-Split.xlsx; Format: .xlsx; Licensing: Internal derivation;
      Geographic Coverage: Mainz (AGS 07315000); Update Frequency: Re-check every
      2.5-5 years; Date Last Updated: 2026-07-22; Updated by: Kausal'
  - name: Interpolation Biomasse und Fluessiggas Mainz 2019-2023
    authority: Kausal
    url:
    description: "Linear interpolation for 2019-2023 between the 2018 Klimaschutzplaner
      values (biomass 77330 MWh, LPG 26997 MWh) and the 2024 chimney-sweep register
      (biomass 33207, LPG 7699), split by each carrier's 2018 sector shares. Replaces
      the plain zeros the Klimaschutzplaner export carries for those years, which
      do not describe a real collapse - biomass ran 77-84 GWh through 2018 and LPG
      27-35 GWh. Datenguete D: no measurement of its own. Replace when the Schornsteinfeger
      register for 2019-2023 arrives.; Format: derived; Licensing: Internal derivation;
      Geographic Coverage: Mainz (AGS 07315000); Update Frequency: Replace when better
      data arrives; Date Last Updated: 2026-08-25; Updated by: Kausal"
  - name: Stadtwerke Mainz Waermepumpenstrom 2019-2024
    authority: Mainzer Stadtwerke AG / Mainzer Netze
    url:
    description: 'Metered heat-pump electricity in the Mainz territory, 2019-2024:
      2508, 3114, 4181, 5055, 4860, 5037 MWh. Converted to delivered heat by the Jahresarbeitszahl
      of 3.2 that the model itself applies (the Leitfaden Datenbeschaffung puts it
      between 2.8 and 3.8 and recommends 3.2). The model books the full delivered
      heat under environmental heat and recovers the electricity from it, so electricity
      x JAZ is the quantity it wants. Sector split taken from the 2018 shares - the
      delivery is a city total. Delivered 2026-06-22 in VERBRAUCH_Strom_Gas_Fernwaerme_Waermepumpen_Nachtspeicher_2019-2024_StadtwerkeMainz_20260622.xlsx.;
      Format: .xlsx; Licensing: Provided to the city for climate accounting; not public;
      Geographic Coverage: Mainz (AGS 07315000); Update Frequency: Annual; Date Last
      Updated: 2026-06-22; Updated by: Mainzer Stadtwerke AG'
  - name: Solarthermie Mainz 2019-2024 (Energieatlas-Index)
    authority: Kausal; based on Energieatlas Rheinland-Pfalz
    url: 
      https://www.energieatlas.rlp.de/earp/daten/waerme/spezialkarte-solarthermie-summe/
    description: 'The 2018 level carried forward in proportion to the growth in funded
      solar collector area recorded by the Energieatlas Rheinland-Pfalz: 4205 m2 in
      2018, 4302 in 2019, 4636 in 2020. NOT the Energieatlas own conversion (area
      x Globalstrahlung x Wirkungsgrad), which covers funded installations only and
      yields about 480 kWh/m2 against the 1210 kWh/m2 the existing series implies
      for 2018 - using it directly would put a factor-2.5 step at 2018/2019. Area
      data ends in 2020, so 2021-2024 hold the 2020 level. Replaces the zeros the
      Klimaschutzplaner export carries. Datenguete D.; Format: .csv; Licensing: Energieatlas
      RLP is public; derivation internal; Geographic Coverage: Mainz (AGS 07315000);
      Update Frequency: Replace when a full installation register is available; Date
      Last Updated: 2026-08-25; Updated by: Kausal'
  - name: Interpolation Heizoel Mainz 2019-2023
    authority: Kausal
    url:
    description: 'Linear interpolation of heating-oil consumption for 2019-2023 between
      the two measured endpoints: 359583 MWh in 2018 (Klimaschutzplaner) and 247107
      MWh in 2024 (chimney-sweep appliance register). Applied per sector; because
      the 2024 sector split already uses the 2018 shares, this is equivalent to interpolating
      the city total and re-splitting it. Datenguete D: these years carry no measurement
      of their own and must rank below the 2024 cells, which are C. Caveat on the
      record: the two endpoints come from different methods - 2018 modelled, 2024
      counted - so part of the decline is an artefact of the method change rather
      than a measured trend. The direction is right (oil heating is being phased out)
      but the slope is not measured. Chosen deliberately over leaving five years empty;
      replace as soon as the Schornsteinfeger register for 2019-2023 arrives.; Format:
      derived; Licensing: Internal derivation; Geographic Coverage: Mainz (AGS 07315000);
      Update Frequency: Replace when better data arrives; Date Last Updated: 2026-08-25;
      Updated by: Kausal'
  - name: EKA-RLP Feuerstaettendaten Mainz 2024
    authority: Energieagentur Rheinland-Pfalz (EKA-RLP) -- Datenlieferservice 
      Kommunales Klimaschutzcontrolling; based on the Schornsteinfeger register
    url:
    description: "Count of heating appliances in Mainz for 2024 by fuel (biomass,
      natural gas, LPG, heating oil, coal) and power class, split into single-room
      stoves and central boilers. Converted to final energy as count x mean power
      x full-load hours using the workbook's own lookup: 8/15 kW at 250 h for single-room
      stoves, 8/18/38/75/150 kW at 1600 h for central boilers (the BISKO / VDI 2067
      default). City totals 2024: heating oil 247107 MWh, biomass 33207 MWh, LPG 7699
      MWh. Applied to natural gas the same method yields 1507765 MWh against EKA-RLP's
      metered 1764236, i.e. 85 percent, so the method under-reads by roughly a sixth.
      The register carries no sector breakdown; the totals are split with each fuel's
      2018 sector shares. Note the sheet holds a second table further down splitting
      biomass into logs, pellets and wood chips, under the same row labels - reading
      past the first block double-counts.; Format: .xlsx; Licensing: Provided to the
      city for climate accounting; not public; Geographic Coverage: Mainz (AGS 07315000);
      Update Frequency: Annual; Date Last Updated: 2026; Updated by: EKA-RLP"
  - name: Stadtwerke Mainz Fernwaerme Territorium 2019-2024
    authority: Mainzer Stadtwerke AG -- Mainzer Fernwaerme GmbH (Simon Reusch) 
      und Mainzer Waerme Plus (Lukas Ritz)
    url:
    description: 'Annual district heating consumption in the Mainz territory by consumer
      sector, as the sum of the Mainzer Fernwaerme GmbH main network and the Mainzer
      Waerme Plus special networks (Lerchenberg, Berliner Siedlung). Main-network
      sector split is an extrapolation from actual customer billing; the special-network
      split applies the sector shares from the Kommunale Waermeplanung Stadtteilsteckbriefe.
      Delivered 2026-06-22 in VERBRAUCH_Strom_Gas_Fernwaerme_Waermepumpen_Nachtspeicher_2019-2024_StadtwerkeMainz_20260622.xlsx.;
      Format: .xlsx; Licensing: Provided to the city for climate accounting; not public;
      Geographic Coverage: Mainz (AGS 07315000); Update Frequency: Annual; Date Last
      Updated: 2026-06-22; Updated by: Mainzer Stadtwerke AG'
  - name: KSP-Export Steinkohle Mainz 2017-2024
    authority: Landeshauptstadt Mainz -- Gruen- und Umweltamt; dedizierte 
      Einzelabfrage im Klimaschutzplaner
    url:
    description: 'Per-carrier KSP query for hard coal (Steinkohle) final energy by
      sector, 2017-2024. 2017-2023 reproduce the existing Klimaschutzplaner sectoral
      figures almost to the decimal; 2024 is the only new column, adding the year
      the model previously held flat. The pre-existing 2019 jump in industrial coal
      (0 to ~54 GWh) remains unexplained -- carried forward, not resolved, by this
      delivery.; Format: xlsx; Licensing: Provided to the city; not public; Geographic
      Coverage: Mainz (AGS 07315000); Update Frequency: Superseded -- single delivery;
      Date Last Updated: 2026-08-25; Updated by: Landeshauptstadt Mainz'
  - name: KSP-Stammdaten Mainz (citymetadata E84)
    authority: Landeshauptstadt Mainz -- amtliche Kreis-Statistik ueber den 
      Klimaschutzplaner
    url:
    description: "Feld 'Energetischer Endenergieverbrauch von Kohle, verarbeitendes
      Gewerbe, Kreis (E84)' aus KSPMainz_citymetadata_19902023.txt, GJ. Verifiziert
      identisch (nach GJ->MWh) mit den bereits im Modell stehenden 2019-2023er Werten
      fuer Steinkohle/Industrie; genutzt, um 2016-2018 nachzutragen, die dieselbe
      Statistik bereits mit echten Werten fuehrt. 1990-2015 bleiben leer, da das Feld
      dort keine Werte hat.; Format: txt; Licensing: Provided to the city; not public;
      Geographic Coverage: Mainz (AGS 07315000); Update Frequency: Superseded -- single
      delivery; Date Last Updated: 2026-08-26; Updated by: Landeshauptstadt Mainz"
  - name: Schornsteinfegerdaten KWP (Kommunale Waermeplanung), Datenabgabe 2025
    authority: Landeshauptstadt Mainz -- Bezirksschornsteinfeger, gesammelt fuer
      die Kommunale Waermeplanung (WPG)
    url:
    description: "Address-free appliance-level register (fuel, rated thermal output,
      central vs. single-room) from 17 chimney-sweep districts, collected Jan-Mar
      2025 (no per-row inspection year; treated as one current-status snapshot applied
      to both 2023 and 2024). Used to replace the EKA-RLP Feuerstaettenzaehlung-based
      estimate for heating_oil, biomass and propane -- preferred per explicit instruction,
      since it is the underlying primary register rather than an already-aggregated
      summary. hard_coal/natural_gas deliberately left on their existing sources (negligible
      register coverage / already grid-metered, respectively). The parallel 'Nach
      PLZ' export of the same register (99.9% address overlap, confirmed) was not
      used, to avoid double-counting.; Format: csv; Licensing: Provided to the city;
      not public; Geographic Coverage: Mainz (AGS 07315000); Update Frequency: Superseded
      -- single delivery; Date Last Updated: 2026-08-26; Updated by: Landeshauptstadt
      Mainz"
  units:
    Value: MWh
    quality: ''
